  [PASS] K6.1 mutation: with the kernel switched off the prediction is wrong by the boost itself, so the agreement is carried by nu(e_N) and not by the geometry   (mean offset moves -0.476 -> +0.095 dex)

  the SENSITIVITY of the prediction to the first law, computed as a derivative rather than assumed:
    d log R_0,pred / d log a_0 = -0.182, NOT the naive -2/3.  Raising a_0 raises H_Lam, which shrinks
    the length scale (G M/H_Lam^2)^(1/3) as a_0^(-2/3), but it also raises H_Lam t_0, which pushes the
    turnaround shell x_ta OUTWARD (x_ta = 0.7175 -> 0.9219 at a_0 x 2).  The two effects
    largely cancel, so the turnaround radius is a WEAK probe of a_0 -- against the candidate's interest.
  [FAIL] K6.2 mutation, restated around what it actually measures: for the candidate to be a test OF a_0, the prediction must be sensitive to a_0.  This check fails if |d log R_0/d log a_0| is far below the naive 2/3, because then a_0 barely appears in the relation at all   (d log R_0,pred/d log a_0 = -0.182 against a naive -0.667; a_0 x 2 moves the mean offset only -0.476 -> -0.384 dex)
  [FAIL] K6.3 mutation: scramble the pairing between each group's radius and its mass.  If the scatter does not grow, the 'law' is only saying that all Local Volume groups are about the same size (bug pattern 5)   (scatter 0.371 dex correctly paired vs 0.324 dex scrambled)

